Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:57:51 +0300
Subject: Game controllers: menus and a fixed race scheme next to the keyboard

SFML 3 on Linux reads /dev/input/js*, so a joystick button is the joydev
index. DualShock 3 (hid-sony): 0 Cross, 1 Circle, 2 Triangle, 3 Square,
4 L1, 5 R1, 6 L2, 7 R2, 9 Start, 13-16 d-pad up/down/left/right; axes X, Y
are the left stick. L2/R2 are buttons there. A pad with no buttons (the
motion sensors) is ignored, and so is every axis but X/Y/PovX/PovY (the old
code took any other axis for "paddle/brake").

State::Manager turns controller events into State::Pad(button, pressed).
The default Pad is the menu: d-pad and left stick are the arrow keys, Cross
and Start Enter, Circle Escape, so every screen with a keyboard path works
with the pad alone. The race overrides Pad:

  left stick (analog) or d-pad    steer
  R2 or R1                        paddle
  L2 or L1                        brake
  Cross                           jump, hold to charge
  Square                          trick (with steer / paddle / brake)
  Triangle                        change view
  Start                           pause

The pad has its own flags next to the keys, so neither cancels the other.
Nothing is written to the options file. Hot-plug is SFML's own events.
The Help screen (keyboard functions) lists the scheme in a second column.

